  "_comment": "Generic example for Acme. Copy into .claude/settings.json (project) or ~/.claude/settings.json (user). Deny rules hold in bypassPermissions and are the layer that stops Bash patterns and MCP writes, which no hook sees; launch.sh refuses to start a bypass run until the baseline is present. Patterns match the whole command with * as a wildcard; they are best effort, so keep the plugin hooks on as well. Merge and protected-branch denials are in settings.deny.non-merge.json: apply them to every role except the integrator and orchestrator.",
